exports[`moduleToText > category-sort: text and markdown snapshots > markdown 1`] = `
"## Who does what at Brightline Media

Sort each activity into the team that owns it. Drag an item into a category, or tap the item and then the category.

### Strategy

Objectives, audiences and the plan

- Translate the client brief into campaign objectives
- Define target audience personas
- Recommend the channel mix and budget split

### Media Buying

Running the money in-platform

- Adjust bids and budgets in the ad platforms
- Choose placements and exclude low-quality inventory

### Analytics

Tracking, measurement and insight

- Install and verify conversion tracking
- Build the weekly performance dashboard
- Pick the attribution model for reporting

### Account Management

The client relationship

- Run the quarterly business review with the client
- Negotiate scope changes and invoicing

Translate the client brief into campaign objectives: Strategy turns the brief into measurable objectives before any channel is chosen.

Adjust bids and budgets in the ad platforms: In-flight bid and budget changes are hands-on-keyboard media buying work.

Install and verify conversion tracking: Analytics owns the tracking stack so that every team reports from the same numbers.

Run the quarterly business review with the client: QBRs are a relationship ritual led by the account team, with input from the others.

Define target audience personas: Personas are a planning artefact that media and creative then act on.

Choose placements and exclude low-quality inventory: Placement selection and brand-safety exclusions are configured by the buyers.

Build the weekly performance dashboard: Dashboards are an analytics deliverable, even though account managers present them.

Negotiate scope changes and invoicing: Commercial conversations about scope and billing sit with account management.

Pick the attribution model for reporting: Attribution is a measurement decision; analytics recommends it, strategy signs it off.

Recommend the channel mix and budget split: The channel mix is a strategic recommendation that media buying then executes.

Hint: Ask who would be blamed if the task went wrong: the planner, the buyer, the analyst or the client lead.

You now know who to ask for what. Expect to hand off work across all four teams in your first month."
`;

