exports[`moduleToText > conversation: text and markdown snapshots > markdown 1`] = `
"## Urgent client message on Friday 5pm

Priya runs marketing at Harbor Supply Co. It is 5:02pm on a Friday and she has just messaged you. Pick the reply you would actually send.

Priya Nair: Marketing Lead, Harbor Supply Co., Online

Priya Nair: Hey, are you still around?

Priya Nair: The spring sale ads are showing the **old 15% code** instead of the 25% one. Our support inbox is filling up and the sale went live an hour ago.

- Proactive: I'm here. Pausing the affected ads now and I'll confirm in 5 minutes which placements had the old code.
- Defensive: That's odd, the brief we got had 15% in it. Can you double check what was sent over?
- Vague: Oh no, sorry to hear that! Let me look into it and get back to you.

I'm here. Pausing the affected ads now and I'll confirm in 5 minutes which placements had the old code.: You answered the question she did not ask: *is anyone handling this?* Concrete action plus a time box lowers her stress immediately.

That's odd, the brief we got had 15% in it. Can you double check what was sent over?: Even if the brief was wrong, 5pm on a Friday with a live sale is not the moment. She hears *not our problem* while customers are seeing the wrong code.

Oh no, sorry to hear that! Let me look into it and get back to you.: Warm but empty. *Get back to you* when? Doing what? With a live problem, the client needs a specific next action.

5 minutes later

Priya Nair: Okay, thank you. I can see spend has stopped.

Priya Nair: It was three of the five ad sets, right? Those are the ones people are complaining about.

- Proactive: Correct, three ad sets. The fix is a creative swap, about 20 minutes to rebuild and resubmit. I'd rather push the right version tonight than leave the sale dark over the weekend. Okay with you?
- Cautious: Yes. I'll fix it Monday first thing so we don't rush changes at this hour.

Correct, three ad sets. The fix is a creative swap, about 20 minutes to rebuild and resubmit. I'd rather push the right version tonight than leave the sale dark over the weekend. Okay with you?: You confirmed the scope, gave an estimate, and offered a recommendation with a reason. Asking for her go-ahead keeps her in control.

Yes. I'll fix it Monday first thing so we don't rush changes at this hour.: Caution is reasonable, but a sale is running *now*. Leaving it paused all weekend turns a 20-minute fix into a lost weekend of revenue.

25 minutes later

Priya Nair: Live again with 25%. Just placed a test order myself, code works.

Priya Nair: Honestly I was dreading this message. Thanks for jumping on it.

- Accountable: Glad it's sorted. I'll send a short note Monday on how the old code slipped through and what we're changing so it doesn't happen again. Enjoy your weekend.
- Friendly: No problem at all! Have a great weekend.

Glad it's sorted. I'll send a short note Monday on how the old code slipped through and what we're changing so it doesn't happen again. Enjoy your weekend.: You closed the loop *and* pre-empted the post-mortem question before she had to ask it. This is how trust is built after a mistake.

No problem at all! Have a great weekend.: Perfectly pleasant, but it leaves the *why did this happen* conversation for Monday, when she may already be asking it.

Saturday, 10:14

Priya Nair: Sale is our biggest weekend of the quarter and ads are off. Can we really not get this live today?

- Accountable: You're right, I should have offered that last night. Rebuilding the three ad sets now, live within the hour.
- Rigid: I can't make changes to live campaigns on weekends without a change request from your side.

You're right, I should have offered that last night. Rebuilding the three ad sets now, live within the hour.: A quick, specific recovery. You lost some goodwill overnight, but owning it without excuses gets most of it back.

I can't make changes to live campaigns on weekends without a change request from your side.: Process is there to protect the client, not to stop you from helping them. Quoting it during their biggest weekend reads as hiding.

Priya Nair: I'm not trying to assign blame, I'm trying to stop customers from seeing the wrong discount.

Priya Nair: Can you pause them or not?

- Accountable: Yes, sorry, pausing the affected ad sets now. I'll confirm in 5 minutes and we can sort out the brief on Monday.
- Defensive: I can, but I want to be clear this wasn't an error on our side.

Yes, sorry, pausing the affected ad sets now. I'll confirm in 5 minutes and we can sort out the brief on Monday.: Good recovery. You dropped the argument and moved to action. Parking the brief question for Monday is the right call.

I can, but I want to be clear this wasn't an error on our side.: Twice defensive. She now has a live problem *and* an agency that seems more worried about fault than fixing it.

20 minutes later

Priya Nair: Any update? Support says 40 tickets now.

- Proactive: Yes. Three of five ad sets had the old code. They're paused as of now and I can have the corrected version live in about 20 minutes if you want me to push it tonight.
- Vague: Still digging into it, will let you know as soon as I have something.

Yes. Three of five ad sets had the old code. They're paused as of now and I can have the corrected version live in about 20 minutes if you want me to push it tonight.: Specific, scoped and actionable. Twenty minutes late, but this is the message she needed from the start.

Still digging into it, will let you know as soon as I have something.: Forty tickets and no action. Vague updates during an incident are worse than silence because they confirm nothing is happening.

Priya Nair: That would be great. Really appreciate it. Have a good one.

You treated an awkward Friday message as a chance to show how the agency behaves under pressure: act first, scope the problem, recommend with a reason, close the loop. Priya will remember the recovery more than the mistake.

Priya Nair: Thanks. Talk Monday.

The problem got fixed and the relationship is intact, but there was room to be faster or more explicit about what happens next. Notice where a specific commitment would have saved a follow-up message.

