- Call to action
- Disclaimer
- Tracking pixel
- Frequency cap

Logo: The logo tells people who is talking before they read a word. Most banners get under two seconds of attention, so brand recognition is often the only thing that sticks — keep it clear and in the same corner across every size.

Headline: The headline carries the one idea of the ad. Three words read at a glance; anything much longer than six tends to be skipped at banner sizes.

Offer: The offer gives a reason to act now. A specific number (−25%) beats vague promises like “great savings”, and it must match what the landing page delivers or the click is wasted.

Product shot: The product shot shows what is being sold and sets the mood. One clear hero product reads better at small sizes than a busy collage.

