exports[`moduleToText > priority-matrix: text and markdown snapshots > markdown 1`] = `
"## Monday morning at Brightline Media

It's 9:05 and you're the account manager on Northwind Outdoor and Harbor Supply Co. Place each task on the matrix: drag it into a quadrant, or tap the task and then the quadrant.

Urgency: low → high

Importance: low → high

### Schedule

Important, not urgent — block time for it

- Draft the Q3 strategy deck for Harbor Supply
- Book training on the new attribution tool

### Do now

Urgent and important — handle it yourself, today

- Tracking is broken on Northwind's live campaign
- Approve creative due to launch at 2pm today

### Drop

Neither — let it go

- Reply to a vendor's newsletter survey
- Tidy the shared drive's archive folder

### Delegate

Urgent, not important — hand it on

- Reformat last week's slides for an internal sync
- Pull a routine weekly export

Tracking is broken on Northwind's live campaign: Every hour without tracking is spend you can't measure or optimise, and the campaign is live. Get Analytics on it before anything else.

Draft the Q3 strategy deck for Harbor Supply: It shapes next quarter's budget, but the review is three weeks away. Block focused time this week so it never becomes an emergency.

Reformat last week's slides for an internal sync: Someone needs it today, but it doesn't need an account manager. A coordinator can turn it around while you deal with the client work.

Reply to a vendor's newsletter survey: No deadline that matters and no effect on any client. Archive it and move on.

Approve creative due to launch at 2pm today: A missed approval delays the launch and the media plan behind it. It's time-bound and client-facing, so it's yours this morning.

Book training on the new attribution tool: Better attribution will change how you report to every client, but nothing breaks if you book it on Wednesday instead of now.

Pull a routine weekly export: Due today, but it follows a fixed recipe. Hand it to the analyst who owns the dashboard — or ask them to automate it.

Tidy the shared drive's archive folder: Satisfying, but neither urgent nor important on a Monday morning. Leave it for a quiet Friday, or for never.

Explanation: Urgency is about the clock; importance is about the client and the business. Do the urgent-and-important work yourself, protect time for the important work before it turns urgent, hand routine urgent tasks to the right person, and give yourself permission to drop the rest.

Run this triage every Monday before you open Slack. It takes two minutes and saves the week."
`;

